,"git_url":"git://github.com/python/mypy.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:python/mypy.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy","homepage":"https://www.mypy-lang.org/","size":77161,"stargazers_count":20064,"watchers_count":20064,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":3065,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3124,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/pulls/19042","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/19042","diff_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/19042.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/19042.patch","merged_at":"2025-07-11T11:27:26Z"},"body":"Fixes #19015. Fixes #17521. Side question: why do we do that extra work to show \"is already defined\" error instead of \"implementation must come last\" in the following setting?\r\n\r\n```python\r\n@overload\r\ndef f2(x: A) -> A: ...\r\nif True:\r\n    @overload\r\n    def f2(x: B) -> B: ...\r\ndef f2(x): ...\r\nif True:\r\n    #@overload  # both with and without this decorator\r\n    def f2(x): ...  # E: Name \"f2\" already defined on line 17\r\n```\r\n\r\nWe have to track it specially and it doesn't work when `f2` is decorated, and I struggle to understand how \"already defined\" is better than an overload-specific message \"implementation must come last\".","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/19042/reactions","tot